## Grammar

### 1. -었으면/았으면/였으면 좋겠다

**Meaning and Usage**
This is used after an action verb or descriptive verb to show the speaker's wishes or hopes. You can also use "하다" in place of "좋겠다."

**Form**
- **'-았으면 좋겠다'** is used when the action or descriptive verb stem ends with 'ㅏ, ㅗ.'
- **'-었으면 좋겠다'** is used when the verb stem ends with another vowel like 'ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ.'
- **'-였으면 좋겠다'** is used when the verb stem ends with '하-' (했으면 좋겠다).

| Action or descriptive verb stem ending | Combine with | Example |
|---|---|---|
| ㅏ, ㅗ | -았으면 좋겠다 | 갔으면 좋겠다, 많았으면 좋겠다 |
| Other vowels (ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ) | -었으면 좋겠다 | 먹었으면 좋겠다, 컸으면 좋겠다 |
| 하 | -였으면 좋겠다 (했으면 좋겠다) | 일했으면 좋겠다, 따뜻했으면 좋겠다 |

**Example**
- 다음 주에 시험이 있습니다. 저는 시험을 잘 봤으면 좋겠습니다. - I have a test next week. I hope I can do well on the test.
- 저는 대학교를 졸업하고 방송국에서 일했으면 좋겠습니다. - After I graduate from college, I hope to work in a broadcasting station.
- 친구가 내일 여행을 가요. 날씨가 좋았으면 좋겠습니다. - My friend is going on a trip tomorrow. I hope the weather is good.
- 룸메이트가 성격이 좋은 사람이었으면 좋겠어요. - I hope my roommate has a good personality.

**가:** 유키 씨, 방학에 무엇을 할 거예요? - Yuki, what will you do during the vacation?
**나:** 저는 외국에 여행을 갔으면 좋겠어요. - I wish I could travel to a foreign country.

**가:** 리타오 씨, 생일에 무슨 선물을 받고 싶어요? - Letao, what kind of gift would you like to receive for your birthday?
**나:** 노트북을 받았으면 좋겠어요. - I would like to receive a notebook.

### 2. -어야겠다/아야겠다/여야겠다

**Meaning and Usage**
This is used after an action verb to show the speaker's strong intention to perform an action he believes is necessary.

**Form**
- **'-아야겠다'** is used when the action verb stem ends with 'ㅏ, ㅗ.'
- **'-어야겠다'** is used when the action verb stem ends with other vowels like 'ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ.'
- **'-여야겠다'(해야겠다)** is used when the action verb stem ends with '하-.'

| Action verb stem | Combine with | Example |
|---|---|---|
| ㅏ, ㅗ | -아야겠다 | 일어나야겠다, 봐야겠다 |
| Other vowels (ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ) | -어야겠다 | 써야겠다, 읽어야겠다 |
| 하 | -여야겠다 (해야겠다) | 공부해야겠다 |

**Example**
- 연필이 없어서 친구에게 빌려야겠습니다. - I don't have a pencil so I should borrow one from a friend.
- 시간이 없어서 저는 택시를 타야겠습니다. - I don't have time so I should take a taxi.
- 다음 주에 시험이 있어서 저는 공부를 해야겠어요. - I have a test next week so I had better study.
- 게임을 너무 많이 하지 말아야겠어요. - I shouldn't play too many games.

**가:** 내일 유키 씨가 이사를 해요. - Yuki is moving tomorrow.
**나:** 그래요? 제가 도와줘야겠어요. - Really? I had better help her.

**가:** 존 씨, 어디 아프세요? - John, are you feeling sick?
**나:** 머리가 아파서 약을 먹어야겠어요. - My head hurts so I should take some medicine.

**Note:** This is used only with action verbs and cannot be used with descriptive verbs.

