## Grammar

### 1. -어/아/여 가지고

**Meaning and Usage**
This is used after an action verb and shows how the result or state of the action mentioned first is maintained until the content that is mentioned later. The result or state of the first action may be the cause or reason for the content that comes later.

**Form**
- **'-아 가지고'** is used when the action verb stem ends with 'ㅏ, ㅗ.'
- **'-어 가지고'** is used when the action verb stem ends with the other vowels 'ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ'
- **'-여 가지고'(해 가지고)** is used when it ends with '하-.'

| Action verb stem ending | Combine with | Example |
|---|---|---|
| ㅏ, ㅗ | -아 가지고 | 사 가지고, 모아 가지고 |
| Other vowels (ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ) | -어 가지고 | 건너 가지고, 만들어 가지고 |
| 하 | -여 가지고 (해 가지고) | 준비해 가지고 |

**Example**
- 당근을 썰어 가지고 프라이팬에 볶으세요. - Cut up the carrot and fry it in the fry pan.
- 한국에서는 집들이에 갈 때 손님들이 휴지를 사 가지고 가요. - When going to a housewarming party in Korea, guests buy toilet paper and bring it.
- 수업에 필요한 것을 준비해 가지고 오세요. - Prepare what you need for class and come.
- 저는 한국어를 열심히 공부해 가지고 한국 회사에 취직하고 싶어요. - I want to diligently study Korean and then get a job at a Korean company.

**가:** 돈을 모아 가지고 뭘 했어요? - What did you do after you saved your money?
**나:** 저는 돈을 모아 가지고 엄마 선물을 샀어요. - I saved my money and bought a gift for my mother.

**가:** 소풍 갈 때 무슨 음식을 가지고 가요? - What food will you bring when you go to the picnic?
**나:** 김밥을 만들어 가지고 갈 거예요. - I will make gimbap and take it to the picnic.

**Note:** This can only be used with action verbs and cannot be used with descriptive verbs. This is usually used in spoken language and can be shortened to '-어/아/여 갖고.'

### 2. -지 마

**Meaning and Usage**
'-지 마' is the informal form of '-지 말다(말아요?, 마세요, 맙시다).' This is used after an action verb to prohibit someone from doing something. Informal form is used when speaking to one's friends or juniors (subordinates) and even very close seniors. The form is the same for questions, commands, and suggestions and is distinguished by intonation.

**Example**
- 여기에서 사진을 찍지 마. - Don't take pictures here.
- 늦게까지 피아노를 치지 마. - Don't play the piano until the late hours.
- 친구에게 그 이야기를 하지 마. - Don't tell your friend that story.
- 음식을 너무 짜게 먹지 마. - Don't eat your food with too much salt.

**가:** 이번 시험이 어려우면 어떻게 하지? - What's going to happen if the upcoming test is difficult?
**나:** 너무 걱정하지 마. 다 잘 될 거야. - Don't worry too much. Everything will work out.

**가:** 더우니까 문을 닫지 마. - Don't close the door because it's hot.
**나:** 알았어요. - Alright.

